tions appearing in print on Thursday, August 1, 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 1, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T03:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/df82772b-0923-55d6-9980-07867dc39e1a', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df82772b-0923-55d6-9980-07867dc39e1a'}, {'abstract': 'All of the candidates onstage closed the nearly three-hour Democratic debate by directing viewers to their websites. All except former Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/us/politics/joe-30330.html', 'snippet': 'All of the candidates onstage closed the nearly three-hour Democratic debate by directing viewers to their websites. All except former Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s among the most routine parts of modern presidential campaigning: a closing plug to visit a campaign website to donate or “find out more.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Go to Joe 30330’: Biden Sends Supporters on a Digital Wild Goose Chase', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T03:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'ne