923-2d5f7c7747de', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e03e107-c7c7-5580-8923-2d5f7c7747de'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not just “Game of Thrones” fans flocking to the Northern Ireland capital; foodies and culture seekers, not to mention history buffs, are finding plenty to keep them busy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/travel/what-to-do-36-hours-in-belfast.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not just “Game of Thrones” fans flocking to the Northern Ireland capital; foodies and culture seekers, not to mention history buffs, are finding plenty to keep them busy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The yellow gantry cranes of Harland & Wolff, the company behind Belfast’s shipbuilding industry and the creation of the Titanic, rise high above the River Lagan and can be seen from nearly everywhere in the city center, a reminder of the working class that built Belfast. As the capital of Northern Ireland — increasingly known for its new restaurants and stimulating galleries — turns its Troubles into tourism, it is fast coming into its own as a European hot spot. Though HBO’s “Game of Thrones” — parts of which were filmed in local studios and nearby areas — deserves credit for helping to put Belfast on the map as a destination, much of the city’s appeal is its warm residents, who are unfailingly ready to share a joke. So build some time into your visit to sink a pint or a cup of third-wave coffee and engage in some impromptu local conversation.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/travel/01Hours-Belfast6/merlin_157852809_9d2853a6-4d00-469a-bcad-734563dd2c69-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Belfast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belfast, Northern Ireland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belfast (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nell McShane Wulfhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nell', 'middlename': 'Mcshane', 'lastname': 'Wulfhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8998146e-89fa-5cb8-969f-669b11cf3da7', 'word_count': 1993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8998146e-89fa-5cb8-969f-669b11cf3da7'}, {'abstract': 'Just 25 minutes from the Acropolis, an alluring stretch of beachfront beckons with island charm. No ferry required.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/travel/five-places-to-visit-athens-riviera.html', 'snippet': 'Just 25 minutes from the Acropolis, an alluring stretch of beachfront beckons with island charm. No ferry required.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The southern coast of Athens, a 35-mile stretch of pine-speckled beachfront, is gaining in popularity for travelers keen on exploring the ruins in the city’s historic center, and then ditching the urban sprawl (it’s a mere 25-minute drive from the Acropolis) for the charms of the Aegean Sea. The ambience of this coastal hideaway, known unofficially as the Athens Riviera, veers more remote Greek island than urban-adjacent beach town.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/merlin_157678806_5215011b-dd3c-42b2-ba40-6aba9e182ad4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/merlin_157678806_5215011b-dd3c-42b2-ba40-6aba9e182ad4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/merlin_157678806_5215011b-dd3c-42b2-ba40-6aba9e182ad4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/merlin_157678806_5215011b-dd3c-42b2-ba40-6aba9e182ad4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/09athens-5places1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/09athens-5places1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/travel/09athens-5places1/09athens-5places1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Places to Visit on the Athens Riviera', 'kicker': '5 places', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All the Charm of an Island, but Without the Ferry Ride', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AEGEAN SEA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T09:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Tara Koch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': 'Tara', 'lastname': 'Koch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/639f628f-b043-5e47-bca0-eb412c765ffd', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/639f628f-b043-5e47-bca0-eb412c765ffd'}, {'abstract': 'The Warroad Pioneer, a pillar of its small Minnesota town, ended its 121-year run with bloody marys, bold type and gloom about the void it would leave behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/us/warroad-pioneer-news-desert.html', 'snippet': 'The Warroad Pioneer, a pillar of its small Minnesota town, ended its 121-year run with bloody marys, bold type and gloom about the void it would leave behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARROAD, Minn. — Whenever she thought her small staff would be facing a particularly stressful deadline day, Rebecca Colden, the publisher of the weekly Warroad Pioneer, declared a Bloody Mary Monday.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dying Gasp of One Local Newspaper', 'kicker': 'The Last Edition', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dying Gasp Of a Local Newspaper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warroad Pioneer (Newspaper)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warroad (Minn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset and Tim Gruber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gruber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6aa56c1-2736-5491-a0d7-1d7e69c58569', 'word_count': 2987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6aa56c1-2736-5491-a0d7-1d7e69c58569'}, {'abstract': 'The Times has not always given the writer his due. Here’s a look at how we covered him and his most famous novel, ‘Moby-Dick,’ over the past century or two.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/books/herman-melville-moby-dick.html', 'snippet': 'The Times has not always given the writer his due. Here’s a look at how we covered him and his most famous novel, ‘Moby-Dick,’ over the past century or two.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Moby-Dick” was published in 1851, but The New York Times didn’t review it. In fact, The Times didn’t mention Herman Melville until 1861 — in a review of somebody else’s book, “Adventures in the South Pacific.” “The author has borrowed bodily, without giving credit therefor, from Melville’s ‘Moby Dick,’” the paper complained, while conceding it was a theft the publisher, “the Harpers, may have sanctioned, as they hold the copyright of both books.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/books/review/01Melville01/merlin_158623956_b749cfb3-46fa-418c-baec-a1badf1027e7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/01/books/review/01Melville01/merlin_158623956_b749cfb3-46fa-418c-baec-a1badf1027e7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 781}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/books/review/01Melville01/merlin_158623956_b749cfb3-46fa-418c-baec-a1badf1027e7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 787, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/books/review/01Melville01/merlin_158623956_b749cfb3-46fa-418c-baec-a1badf1027e7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1574, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '