: None, 'lastname': 'Yuhas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moses', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6717b67c-198b-58fa-b8b1-4132cad12faa', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6717b67c-198b-58fa-b8b1-4132cad12faa'}, {'abstract': 'Elegant and artful, “The Day,” with choreography by Lucinda Childs, feels inadequate to the event to which it responds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/arts/dance/review-wendy-whelan-maya-beiser-lucinda-childs.html', 'snippet': 'Elegant and artful, “The Day,” with choreography by Lucinda Childs, feels inadequate to the event to which it responds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BECKET, Mass. — The dancer Wendy Whelan and the cellist Maya Beiser are towering figures in their respective fields. But in their multimedia collaboration “The Day,” they are overshadowed by another pair. It’s not the project’s two behind-the-scenes luminaries: David Lang, who wrote the music, and Lucinda Childs, who did the choreography. The pair whose absence looms over everything is the twin towers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/merlin_158735295_32a349a2-cd17-4caa-b434-dd3b68908b43-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/merlin_158735295_32a349a2-cd17-4caa-b434-dd3b68908b43-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/merlin_158735295_32a349a2-cd17-4caa-b434-dd3b68908b43-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/merlin_158735295_32a349a2-cd17-4caa-b434-dd3b68908b43-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/01whelan-pillow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/01whelan-pillow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/arts/01whelan-pillow/01whelan-pillow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Wendy Whelan and Maya Beiser’s Meditation on 9/11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Meditation on 9/11, Draped in Stylishness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Jacob's Pillow Dance Festival", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'THE DAY (Dance)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beiser, Maya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Childs, Lucinda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whelan, Wendy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T19:03:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb327d41-11a8-5675-912f-40174ad2044f', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb327d41-11a8-5675-912f-40174ad2044f'}, {'abstract': 'At least 112 pro-government forces and 69 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during the past week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/magazine/afghan-war-casualty-report.html', 'snippet': 'At least 112 pro-government forces and 69 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during the past week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least 112 pro-government forces and 69 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during the past week. The deadliest attacks took place in Farah Province, where a passenger bus traveling from was hit by a roadside bomb in Balaboluk District, killing at least 35 civilians, women and children among them, and wounding more than a dozen others. Elsewhere, a Taliban attack in the Belcheragh District of Faryab Province resulted in the deaths of eight commandos and 14 members of the territorial army. In Kandahar Province, two American soldiers were killed in an insider attack. The attacker was arrested and is currently in the custody of the United States forces in Afghanistan. Earlier this week, the United Nations announced in a report that nearly 1,400 civilians in Afghanistan have died in the first six months of 2019, attributing 52% of those deaths to Afghan forces and their allies, whose reliance on aerial operations has had particularly lethal effects on civilians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/01/magazine/1atwar-casualtyreport-1/merlin_158633187_fed3c419-0f49-49f9-a0db-ee24afbd0e52-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge',