on': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97ef8fe9-9e77-56b5-9f8a-50ecb65db183', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97ef8fe9-9e77-56b5-9f8a-50ecb65db183'}, {'abstract': 'He saw a void in the 1950s and filled it with coverage of colleges and universities. Today the publication reaches a wide readership online and in print.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/obituaries/corbin-gwaltney-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He saw a void in the 1950s and filled it with coverage of colleges and universities. Today the publication reaches a wide readership online and in print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corbin Gwaltney, whose groundbreaking newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education penetrated the nation’s ivory towers and even turned a profit, died on Monday at his home in Potomac, Md. He was 97.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/merlin_158684796_cb239916-3cd8-44da-aad3-e82318f89fff-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/merlin_158684796_cb239916-3cd8-44da-aad3-e82318f89fff-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/merlin_158684796_cb239916-3cd8-44da-aad3-e82318f89fff-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/merlin_158684796_cb239916-3cd8-44da-aad3-e82318f89fff-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/31Gwaltney01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/31Gwaltney01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/obituaries/31Gwaltney01/31Gwaltney01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Corbin Gwaltney, Chronicle of Higher Education Founder, Dies at 97', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corbin Gwaltney, 97, Founder of an Ivory Tower Must-Read', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gwaltney, Corbin (1922-2019)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chronicle of Higher Education', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-01T20:47:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b0f4866-592b-54bd-9599-75ac1ac390bb', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b0f4866-592b-54bd-9599-75ac1ac390bb'}, {'abstract': 'The Art Institute of Chicago explores the great paradox of the 19th century’s greatest painter: from a scandalous youth of frank nudes to flowers, fruit bowls and fashionable women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/01/arts/design/manet-modern-beauty-review-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The Art Institute of Chicago explores the great paradox of the 19th century’s greatest painter: from a scandalous youth of frank nudes to flowers, fruit bowls and fashionable women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — I wonder how often he thought back on it: the outrage, the reproaches, the shame, the folly. In 1865, two years after they rejected his “Déjeuner sur l’herbe,” the gatekeepers of the Paris Salon accepted two paintings by Édouard Manet into Europe’s most prestigious exhibition. One was a slablike, Spanish-influenced religious scene of Christ mocked by Roman legionaries. But it was the other that eclipsed more than 3,500 other works in the Salon, and set off a scandal that makes the recent brouhaha at the Whitney Biennial look as stately as a Noh drama.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/arts/25manet-review/merlin_158257107_37b27962-9242-42ab-947d-5b9810c0676c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/25/arts/25manet-review/merlin_158257107_37b27962-9242-42ab-947d-5b9810c0676c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/arts/25manet-review/merlin_158257107_37b27962-9242-42ab-947d-5b9810c0676c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/arts/25manet-review/merlin_158257107_37b27962-9242-42ab-947d-5b9810c0676c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1556, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,