b126-a279a763c1a6'}, {'abstract': 'Blink and you’ll miss this Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon acrostic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/03/crosswords/variety-acrostic.html', 'snippet': 'Blink and you’ll miss this Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon acrostic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ACROSTIC — Today’s excerpt is from a book by a Times writer and editor, Alan Burdick, called “Why Time Flies: A Mostly Scientific Investigation.” I’m no expert, but I believe that the notion of time, or “temporal consciousness,” is integral to consciousness in general, a concept that’s been addressed in previous passages selected by Team Cox/Rathvon (I am thinking of a recent Michael Pollan excerpt but there have been others). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Emily (Crossword Constructor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burdick, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rathvon, Henry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-03T15:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b4454fb-03c4-50d9-80fa-ef2cb9ea7b10', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b4454fb-03c4-50d9-80fa-ef2cb9ea7b10'}, {'abstract': 'Wild dogs have returned to the famed Gorongosa National Park in Mozambique. The first puppy litters were not far behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/03/science/african-dogs-pups-gorongosa.html', 'snippet': 'Wild dogs have returned to the famed Gorongosa National Park in Mozambique. The first puppy litters were not far behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last summer, not long after releasing a pioneer pack of 14 African wild dogs into Mozambique’s Gorongosa National Park as part of an ambitious wildlife restoration effort, Paola Bouley went to see for herself what in the name of Canis major could have happened to the wild dog pups.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/science/05SCI-DOGS1b/05SCI-DOGS1b-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}]