ations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darusman, Marzuki', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Min Aung Hlaing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-05T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard C. Paddock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Paddock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c918e5b8-f17e-5259-81f6-249c6d6756bb', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c918e5b8-f17e-5259-81f6-249c6d6756bb'}, {'abstract': 'In a new comedy on Netflix, three mothers reconnect with their grown sons. And Olivier Assayas’s latest movie is on Hulu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/05/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday-otherhood-and-non-fiction.html', 'snippet': 'In a new comedy on Netflix, three mothers reconnect with their grown sons. And Olivier Assayas’s latest movie is on Hulu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTHERHOOD (2019) Stream on Netflix. A lesson for sons with mothers who expect them to get in touch on Mother’s Day: Call, don’t text. Otherwise you might set your mother up for the kind of retort Patricia Arquette’s character has in this movie when her adult son (played by Jake Hoffman) replies “I texted” to her complaint that he didn’t call her on Mother’s Day. The line she slams back with? “I birthed you.” They’re not the only baggage-laden mother-son pairing here; the comedy brings together a trio of moms who journey to New York to reconnect with their children. The film was written and directed by Cindy Chupack, whose past as a writer and executive producer of “Sex and the City” increasingly pokes through as the three women travel from the suburbs to the city. The two other mothers are played by Angela Bassett and Felicity Huffman, whose involvement in the recent college admission scandal may taint this breezy movie.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/arts/05tvcol-otherhood/merlin_158745837_8df290fb-250b-47b3-b0fb-b1ae6abf3bdb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop