: 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4d724de-9671-5841-8ec0-2bd1a6e5c36f', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4d724de-9671-5841-8ec0-2bd1a6e5c36f'}, {'abstract': 'Gravensteins fed the armed forces in the 1940s, and now you can try one, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/05/dining/gravenstein-apple.html', 'snippet': 'Gravensteins fed the armed forces in the 1940s, and now you can try one, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back during World War II, when the Gravenstein apple was not considered an heirloom variety, apple sauce made from them fed the American armed forces. There were more than 10,000 acres of Gravensteins grown in California in those days, now down to about 700 acres in Sonoma County, Calif. It’s an early season apple, available for just two weeks in August. Boxes of the tart-sweet red and green-skinned apples are now available nationally, with 16 percent of the price going to support research to increase harvests.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/merlin_158743716_d2bf755e-b03d-4550-9e1c-a69d78603786-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/merlin_158743716_d2bf755e-b03d-4550-9e1c-a69d78603786-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/merlin_158743716_d2bf755e-b03d-4550-9e1c-a69d78603786-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/merlin_158743716_d2bf755e-b03d-4550-9e1c-a69d78603786-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/05burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/05burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner5/05burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A World War II Apple Stages a Comeback', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Relish: A World War II Apple  Stages a Comeback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sonoma County (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-05T16:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8f03404-33db-5ccf-ab0a-db54cdeb8cff', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8f03404-33db-5ccf-ab0a-db54cdeb8cff'}, {'abstract': 'Sylvia Weinstock will share tales from her storied wedding cake career at the Museum at Eldridge Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/05/dining/sylvia-weinstock-talk-cakes.html', 'snippet': 'Sylvia Weinstock will share tales from her storied wedding cake career at the Museum at Eldridge Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sylvia Weinstock, the Fabergé of wedding cakes, is 89 and still at it, fashioning stupendous special-occasion confections. She will be at the Museum at Eldridge Street to talk about her life and loves and help celebrate Tu B’Av, a holiday that’s like a Jewish Valentine’s Day. There will be music, food, drinks and readings of love letters.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/merlin_158700429_de265a51-dead-47b8-8c0a-e85f420544c0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/merlin_158700429_de265a51-dead-47b8-8c0a-e85f420544c0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/merlin_158700429_de265a51-dead-47b8-8c0a-e85f420544c0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 935, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/merlin_158700429_de265a51-dead-47b8-8c0a-e85f420544c0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 935, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/05burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/05burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner1/05burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cake Maven Spills Her Secrets', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Marvel: Cake Maven  Spills Her Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstock, Sylvia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum at Eldridge Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-05T16:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79c1b329-7011-5eb3-afce-58cbadabe9ec', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79c1b329-7011-5eb3-afce-58cbadabe9ec'}, {'abstract': 'Four Winters uses liquid nitrogen to freeze traditional favorites and some intriguing flavors like cereal crunch and knafeh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/05/dining/four-winters-ice-cream.html', 'snippet': 'Four Winters uses liquid nitrogen to freeze traditional favorites and some intriguing flavors like cereal crunch and knafeh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Molecular gastronomy’s contribution to summertime treats is instant ice cream, emerging, like magic, in a puff of smoke. Nitrogen gas, which liquefies at an extremely low temperature, can freeze ingredients, like cream, on contact, an effect that chefs like Heston Blumenthal, of the Fat Duck in England, have used to stunning effect. Some ice cream shops, including Four Winters, a new ice cream shop in Queens, use the same technique. A narrow storefront, this English import has an open kitchen, ingredients on view and seating. The ice cream is churned for each order: The results are ultrasmooth since the quick freeze keeps the ice crystals from forming. Basic flavors are chocolate, vanilla, brown sugar, sweet cream and vegan chocolate, with housemade mix-in options. Specialty varieties include Key lime pie, cereal crunch, vegan chocolate peanut butter and spectacular s’mores. The most popular is knafeh, with pistachios and bits of kadayif, reflecting the Middle Eastern origins of the founders, Omar Alkhawaja, Zeid Zabian and Zaynab Abdullah. Christy Jorsling is the executive chef.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner7/merlin_158767173_1c313b2f-f9cf-4e1e-b63b-fc8b5eee9581-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner7/merlin_158767173_1c313b2f-f9cf-4e1e-b63b-fc8b5eee9581-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner7/merlin_158767173_1c313b2f-f9cf-4e1e-b63b-fc8b5eee9581-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/dining/05burner7/merlin_158767173_1c313b2f-f9cf-4e1e-b63b-fc8b5eee9581-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capti