yt://article/5e8bf47f-9caf-5a34-b982-a2c431f4c6b3', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8bf47f-9caf-5a34-b982-a2c431f4c6b3'}, {'abstract': 'Determine whether the rhythm is steady or sporadic. A whistling before the pop is another giveaway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/06/magazine/how-to-tell-gunfire-from-fireworks.html', 'snippet': 'Determine whether the rhythm is steady or sporadic. A whistling before the pop is another giveaway.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Listen for the cadence,” says Scott Beisner, a public-safety specialist for ShotSpotter, which has installed acoustic sensors in more than 100 cities to capture and locate where shots are fired. “When somebody pulls a trigger, they tend to pull it in a fairly steady rhythm until the end, when their finger gets tired,” Beisner says. A series of evenly spaced bang-bang-bang sounds is much more likely to be a gun than the more sporadic ba-bang, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang of firecrackers. When sensors record a gunlike noise in, say, Cape Town or Chicago, software analyzes it for the sonic signatures of gunfire, and within seconds Beisner and his team listen to those audio files and look at those recorded waveforms at their office in Newark, Calif. Confirmed or suspected gunfire incidents are then reported to the local police.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 556}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 949, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1898, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11Mag-Tip-1/11Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Tell Gunfire From Fireworks', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Tell Gunfire From Fireworks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fireworks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-06T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a9ed7d4-7d6b-55f2-9c33-9713b1289091', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a9ed7d4-7d6b-55f2-9c33-9713b1289091'}, {'abstract': 'A trade war spills into the realm of currency, with no end in sight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/06/upshot/china-us-trade-war-currency-markets.html', 'snippet': 'A trade war spills 