, 'print_headline': 'The Messianic Pragmatist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Karl Marx: Philosophy and Revolution (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marx, Karl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AVINERI, SHLOMO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Communism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-06T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d42f8a2e-e2ce-58c5-9070-c789baae5fbc', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d42f8a2e-e2ce-58c5-9070-c789baae5fbc'}, {'abstract': 'A Filipino staple passed down through the generations since World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/06/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-spam.html', 'snippet': 'A Filipino staple passed down through the generations since World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can’t say that I grew up eating that much Spam. In our house, it was a treat, something my mother would fry up when my father was out and serve — in the Filipino way — with rice. My mother was an excellent cook and believed in fresh ingredients, but Spam was an exception. Occasionally she would also roll out a can of creamed corn, adding milk and sugar to transform it into a kind of dessert. Once in a long while, a can of condensed milk would appear, and my sister and I would be invited to spread it on bread, or even eat it straight from the can with a spoon. As with so many of my mother’s parenting choices, the cooking of the Spam and its tinned brethren had a rich history that she chose not to share. But of these foods, the only one that I still like — and have passed on to my children — is Spam.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/magazine/11mag-lor/11mag-lor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Spam', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spam', 'name': Non