alue': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-07T13:42:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kai Schultz, Suhasini Raj and Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Suhasini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5505e537-f630-541f-8d8a-92bbdbe7b456', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5505e537-f630-541f-8d8a-92bbdbe7b456'}, {'abstract': 'An author looks back on “Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark,” a book series that terrified him as a child and inspired him as an adult.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/07/movies/scary-stories-del-toro-ovredal.html', 'snippet': 'An author looks back on “Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark,” a book series that terrified him as a child and inspired him as an adult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When our son learned to walk, he nearly destroyed our home. Using a tabletop to pull himself to his feet, he might snag on a lamp wire and send it smashing to the ground. Once on his feet, he’d trot across the living room, wobbly as a foal, then slam into the far wall and cause a painting to buckle and fall. On one of those occasions I imagined a book based on a child like ours. The story would be about a boy whose greatest joy came from demolishing his surroundings. He had the power to remove his own head and throw it at things. Even better, the head exploded like a bomb. Then he’d grow a new head and have the same fun all over again. I’d call it “The Adventures of Kenny Kaboom.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/merlin_158699211_6389ad5c-b0c1-490b-a1f4-8f1e463d09bd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/merlin_158699211_6389ad5c-b0c1-490b-a1f4-8f1e463d09bd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/merlin_158699211_6389ad5c-b0c1-490b-a1f4-8f1e463d09bd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/merlin_158699211_6389ad5c-b0c1-490b-a1f4-8f1e463d09bd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/11scary-stories-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/11scary-stories-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11scary-stories-sub/11scary-stories-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', '