8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b643b2f1-3dfb-548e-b69d-124711129e0a'}, {'abstract': 'From members-only clubs to women-only co-working spaces, there are plenty of private enclaves for Angelenos to choose from in 2019.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/07/style/private-clubs-los-angeles.html', 'snippet': 'From members-only clubs to women-only co-working spaces, there are plenty of private enclaves for Angelenos to choose from in 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Private social clubs would seem to be a perfect match for Los Angeles, where the best parties usually happen behind closed doors. But until recently, the main game in town was the Jonathan Club, which was founded in 1895 and barely registered among the young, dewier set. Everything changed in 2010, when Soho House opened in West Hollywood and became a see-and-be-seen hangout for Hollywood deal makers. Now, a surge of members-only clubs (many from London) are opening across L.A., appealing to enclaves as diverse as the city itself. Here are six of the buzziest.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/08/fashion/00privateLAclub-main-sub/00privateLAclub-main-sub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/08/fashion/00privateLAclub-main-sub/00privateLAclub-main-sub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/08/fashion/00privateLAclub-main-sub/00privateLAclub-main-sub-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/08/fashion/00privateLAclub-main-sub/00privateLAclub-main-sub-superJumb