ue': 'Boeing 737 Max Groundings and Safety Concerns (2019)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-07T15:34:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Letters', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/43067265-8991-55f7-b102-b9a7ac2907b3', 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43067265-8991-55f7-b102-b9a7ac2907b3'}, {'abstract': 'Why trade war scares the market so much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/07/opinion/tariff-tantrums-and-recession-risks.html', 'snippet': 'Why trade war scares the market so much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the bond market is any indication, Donald Trump’s escalating belligerence on trade is creating seriously increased risks of recession. But I haven’t seen many clear explanations of why that might be so. The problem isn’t just, or even mainly, that he really does seem to be a Tariff Man. What’s more important is that he’s a capricious, unpredictable Tariff Man. And that capriciousness is really bad for business investment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/reader-center/-070819krugmanblog-web/05now-fedres-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/05/reader-center/-070819krugmanblog-web/05now-fedres-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/reader-center/-070819krugmanblog-web/05now-fedres-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'ju