,” Rochefort says on an afternoon in June. And besides, with works in progress for his first institutional show, “Absorption by the Sun,” which opened Aug. 1 at the Museum of Contemporary Art Santa Barbara, he explains, “I’m running out of room.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN/05tmag-rochefort-slide-U9VN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sculptor Who Makes Ceramics Inspired by Volcanoes', 'kicker': 'T Presents', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sculpture; Master of Blobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Doren Waxter (Manhattan, NY, Gallery)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rochefort, Brian (1985- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-07T16:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janelle Zara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60938381-0850-5ee8-9cc8-9b52402d7fd5', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60938381-0850-5ee8-9cc8-9b52402d7fd5'}, {'abstract': 'Tomi Ahmed, the co-founder of the emerging fragrance brand Iiuvo, believes that every scent has a soundtrack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/07/t-magazine/tomi-ahmed-iiuvo.html', 'snippet': 'Tomi Ahmed, the co-founder of the emerging fragrance brand Iiuvo, believes that every scent has a soundtrack.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I could play you a track to tell you how it smells,” says Tomi Ahmed, the co-founder of Iiuvo, an experimental fragrance brand that tests the limits of what a perfume can be. The 29-year-old is describing Woodgrain, one of a trio of scented candles that kick-started the company he set up with his friend Leo Gibbon in 2015. Wearing a subtly frayed Celine suit with black Birkenstocks and a Chicago White Sox cap, Ahmed lists the references behind the sultry blend of cardamom, myrrh and tonka bean: the Texas rapper Bun B, Iceberg Slim’s 1967 memoir “Pimp: The Story of My Life” and the woody interior of a Cadillac. “It’s amazing the layers of influences that go into just creating a candle,” Amed says of the scent, which was designed to evoke Southern rap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P/05tmag-ahmed-slide-G23P-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumb