: None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epstein, Jeffrey E (1953- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staley, James E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-08T14:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Flitter and Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flitter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a80ac739-c417-5f66-9ec3-78e760986dde', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a80ac739-c417-5f66-9ec3-78e760986dde'}, {'abstract': 'The Silver Jews and Purple Mountains leader, who wrote beloved, endlessly quotable tracks, died at 52.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/08/arts/music/david-berman-silver-jews-playlist.html', 'snippet': 'The Silver Jews and Purple Mountains leader, who wrote beloved, endlessly quotable tracks, died at 52.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Like a message broadcast on an overpass,” David Berman once sang, “all my favorite singers couldn’t sing.” It wasn’t Berman’s forte either, and rather than try to sweeten his crooked croak, he took a deadpan approach to his music, which was consumed with classic literary themes: death, family, booze, escaping fate and finality. Berman, who died on Wednesday at 52, occupied a cultural midpoint between Townes Van Zandt and Raymond Carver, and his imagistic, lively, endlessly quotable lyrics always had a cleverness buoying the emotional struggles and glimpses of life at the margins. Here are 12 of his essential songs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 569}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 971, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1942, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/09/arts/08berman-playlist/08berman-playlist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Berman’s Essential Songs: Listen to 12 Tracks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emotional Struggles Led to Essential Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berman, David (1967-2019)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Jews', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-08T14:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Tannenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tannenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1185d60-e9d0-547e-b50e-a54d34ef57c6', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1185d60-e9d0-547e-b50e-a54d34ef57c6'}, {'abstract': 'A reader wonders why her ex-stepmother’s mother doesn’t lavish her with gifts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/08/style/divorce-step-grandmother.html', 'snippet': 'A reader wonders why her ex-stepmother’s mother doesn’t lavish her with gifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I met my step-grandmother (the mother of my stepmom) when I was 4. She didn’t have any other grandchildren at the time, and I thought she considered me family. But 14 and 11 years ago, when my stepmother’s daughters were born, it became clear that I was a second-class grandchild. It didn’t help matters when my stepmom and father divorced. One year, for instance, my stepsisters got pearls for Christmas, and I got a dish towel. I’ve told my stepmother how bad this makes me feel, but she hasn’t done anything to fix the situation. Should I speak to my step-grandmother?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions of a ‘Second-Class Grandchild’', 'kicker': 'SOCIAL Q’S', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘I Got a Dish Towel’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separatio