k': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fentanyl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-09T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40ef34cf-8047-5be9-bf14-77b0705d4a2b', 'word_count': 2874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40ef34cf-8047-5be9-bf14-77b0705d4a2b'}, {'abstract': 'Once the scope of the festival became clear, The New York Times scrambled to cover its significance. Shakespeare was quoted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/09/arts/music/woodstock-new-york-times-archives.html', 'snippet': 'Once the scope of the festival became clear, The New York Times scrambled to cover its significance. Shakespeare was quoted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times, which the year before had become the first mainstream newspaper to hire a full-time rock critic, initially sent just one reporter to cover the festival in August of 1969. As Arthur Gelb, then the metropolitan editor and the paper’s culture czar, wrote decades later in his memoir, “City Room,” he had expected Woodstock to be “just another big music festival,” like the Newport jazz and folk festivals. When that reporter, Barnard L. Collier, got to Bethel, N.Y., on that Friday, he encountered enormous traffic jams as hundreds of thousands of people descended on Max Yasgur’s farm. But it took a phone call from one of Gelb’s younger reporters, Grace Lichtenstein, imploring him to send more people to cover the festival, saying “this story is much bigger than The Times thinks it is.”', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1195, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-archive/11woodstock-archive-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Woodstock 1969: A Story Vastly Bigger Than Editors Realized', 'kicker': 'Woodstock AT 50', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Story Vastly Bigger Than Editors Realized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Woodstock Music Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Arthur', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reeves, Richard (1936- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-09T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lorne Manly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lorne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49e1a56c-af22-554e-8e01-0e20e474d6a3', 'word_count': 2091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49e1a56c-af22-554e-8e01-0e20e474d6a3'}, {'abstract': 'Six movies, 12 album collections, two songs and 17 books that will take willing travelers back to August 1969 — mud not included.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/09/arts/music/woodstock-movies-albums-books.html', 'snippet': 'Six movies, 12 album collections, two songs and 17 books that will take willing travelers back to August 1969 — mud not included.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Woodstock” (1970)', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-guide06/11woodstock-guide06-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/11/arts/11woodstock-guide06/11woodstock-guide06-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima