n': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/fashion/09SCENE-slide-DBS7/09SCENE-slide-DBS7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Polo in the Hamptons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southampton Hospital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brinkley, Christie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-09T14:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Style', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denny Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4beca5df-4853-53b1-ae39-a382a1d6f509', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4beca5df-4853-53b1-ae39-a382a1d6f509'}, {'abstract': 'She returned to us again and again, wrote book after book for us, about us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/09/opinion/sunday/i-was-wandering-toni-morrison-found-me.html', 'snippet': 'She returned to us again and again, wrote book after book for us, about us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the Bible was the only book I remember my grandmother owning. It was leather-bound and wide, so big that she’d had someone build a wooden stand for it, and she set it up in its permanent home in the corner of her pine-walled living room, atop a corner table. Even though I could not yet read, I sought it out; I sat on the edge of the sofa, my bony 5-year-old chest flush with the wispy, tissue thin paper, and I ran my fingers across the pages, down the psalms. Reproductions of famous paintings appeared every hundred pages or so, colorful depictions of the stories of the Old and New Testaments enticing me even more. I sat beside the wood-burning stove that heated the house, my skin and scalp prickling, the side of my face burning, as I pored over the pages, yearning to understand the words, the stories.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1525, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/11/opinion/sunday/11Ward/11Ward-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Was Wandering. Toni Morrison Found Me.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Was Wandering. Toni Morrison Found Me.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrison, Toni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-09T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesmyn Ward', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesmyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ward', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/29ba2303-7a1c-5ea0-9bca-cddbcd5e691d', 'word_count': 1540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29ba2303-7a1c-5ea0-9bca-cddbcd5e691d'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty years ago, novels by Jacqueline Susann, Mario Puzo and Philip Roth topped the best-seller list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/09/books/review/inside-the-list-1969-best-sellers.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty years ago, novels by Jacqueline Susann, Mario Puzo and Philip Roth topped the best-seller list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the height of the beach-reading season — usually a time when there are new titles scrapping for the No. 1 slots each week — but this summer, things have been, well, not quite as lively. Delia Owens’s “Where the Crawdads Sing” is once again the top-selling novel, as it has been for most of the year, and Tara Westover’s memoir, “Educated,” remains ensconced at No. 1 on the nonfiction list. So to spice things up, we looked back to the summer of 1969 to see what people were reading 50 years ago.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20