'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Vigdor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vigdor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8e70cb2-2f30-5f76-bcd3-4fa6601f67ea', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8e70cb2-2f30-5f76-bcd3-4fa6601f67ea'}, {'abstract': 'The president became frustrated over his news coverage and his angry reaction led to White House-distributed media that focused on him, not people affected by the shootings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/09/us/politics/trump-dayton-el-paso-shootings.html', 'snippet': 'The president became frustrated over his news coverage and his angry reaction led to White House-distributed media that focused on him, not people affected by the shootings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — By the time President Trump arrived in El Paso on Wednesday, on the second leg of a trip to meet with people affected by mass shootings in two cities, he was frustrated that his attacks on his political adversaries had resulted in more coverage than the cheery reception he received at a hospital in Dayton, Ohio, the first stop on his trip. So he screamed at his aides to begin producing proof that in El Paso people were happy to see him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/10/us/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1/10dc-trumpvisit-sub1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Trip to Dayton and El Paso: The Back Story', 'kicker': 'White House Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thumbs Up and All Smiles, the President Strains to Send a Message', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'El Paso, Tex, Shooting (2019)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dayton, Ohio, Shooting (2019)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anchondo, Paul (2019- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anchondo, Jordan (1994-2019)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-10T01:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 