dings will be either boring or extremely dangerous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/10/opinion/sunday/are-we-living-in-a-computer-simulation-lets-not-find-out.html', 'snippet': 'Experimental findings will be either boring or extremely dangerous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the 1990s, researchers in the social and natural sciences have used computer simulations to try to answer questions about our world: What causes war? Which political systems are the most stable? How will climate change affect global migration? The quality of these simulations is variable, since they are limited by how well modern computers can mimic the vast complexity of our world — which is to say, not very well.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We Living in a Computer Simulation? Let’s Not Find Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Are We Living in a Computer Simulation?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-10T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Preston Greene', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Preston', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greene', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/24fbfc80-3746-50b7-9e16-d62b87b12e69', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24fbfc80-3746-50b7-9e16-d62b87b12e69'}, {'abstract': 'Just look at history. Or at my inbox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/10/opinion/hate.html', 'snippet': 'Just look at history. Or at my inbox.', 'lead_paragra