ees Swarm Berlin, Where Beekeeping Is Booming', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Swarms Collapse Worldwide, Amateur Beekeepers Keep Berlin Awash in Hives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biodiversity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-11T14:27:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze and Palko Karasz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Palko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karasz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64d22d65-8132-5d7b-975c-6f371a095b09', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64d22d65-8132-5d7b-975c-6f371a095b09'}, {'abstract': 'David Tanis’s latest is a twist on the classic, using summer vegetables and topping them with a tahini dressing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/11/dining/a-superb-mixed-grill.html', 'snippet': 'David Tanis’s latest is a twist on the classic, using summer vegetables and topping them with a tahini dressing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. We’re hurtling through the season now, “the best of the summer gone and the new fall not yet born,” is how Sylvia Plath put it in her journal. “The odd uneven time.” We’re waiting on the corn from the patch by the harbor, for the better tomatoes to come in alongside the tiny little eggplants, for the