7377d67d0'}, {'abstract': 'Maille, a French mustard company, has added rosé de Provence to a Dijon-style limited edition, seasonal condiment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/12/dining/rose-wine-mustard.html', 'snippet': 'Maille, a French mustard company, has added rosé de Provence to a Dijon-style limited edition, seasonal condiment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The inevitability of rosé in summer goes beyond bottles of wine. This summer Maille (pronounced my), a French mustard company, has added rosé de Provence and a touch of grapefruit (pink, one might assume) to its Dijon-style mustard for a limited-edition seasonal condiment. The result is mellow and rich, with a touch of citrus that calls for some silky cooked ham on baguette. It comes in a nice stoneware crock, and would elevate a vinaigrette. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 792}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1552, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner2/12burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosé Is Everywhere, Including in Mustard', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Season: A Summer Mustard That’s Mellow and Rich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mustard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-12T16:35:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e434d9c3-6c8e-5445-a82f-0d29e4706a00', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e434d9c3-6c8e-5445-a82f-0d29e4706a00'}, {'abstract': 'Vienna Cookie Company in Baldwin, N.Y., added this specialty to their inventory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/12/dining/austrian-poppy-seed-cake.html', 'snippet': 'Vienna Cookie Company in Baldwin, N.Y., added this specialty to their inventory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heidi Riegler, the founder and a baker of Vienna Cookie Company in Baldwin, N.Y., has just added a new Austrian specialty to her inventory. It’s a classic poppy seed cake, or mohntorte, a confection that was her favorite when she was growing up in Vienna. The cake is deliciously dense with poppy seeds and comes blanketed with marzipan. When the weather cools, she plans to glaze it with chocolate. The cake comes in four-, six- and eight-inch sizes. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/merlin_158659848_6db056d6-8aba-4862-ad98-b6c7aa708c17-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/merlin_158659848_6db056d6-8aba-4862-ad98-b6c7aa708c17-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/merlin_158659848_6db056d6-8aba-4862-ad98-b6c7aa708c17-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/merlin_158659848_6db056d6-8aba-4862-ad98-b6c7aa708c17-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/12burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/12burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/12burner3/12burner3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reward Yourself With Austrian Poppy Seed Cake', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: Poppy Seed Cakes Are Your Reward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-12T16:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efa1864b-e81b-5b05-b19d-303cc3cf31e6', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efa1864b-e81b-5b05-b19d-303cc3cf31e6'}, {'abstract': 'Kashmir’s newspapers, cut off from technology by the Indian government, are rising to the occasion to serve readers desperate for information in the war-torn region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/12/world/asia/kashmir-crackdown-newspapers.html', 'snippet': 'Kashmir’s newspapers, cut off from technology by the Indian government, are rising to the occasion to serve readers desperate for information in the war-torn region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SRINAGAR, Kashmir — Ever since Kashmir’s autonomy was suddenly revoked last week, Raja Mohi-ud-din, an editor at one of the few Kashmiri newspapers still operating, has been starting his days extremely early.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/12/world/12kashmir1/merlin_159180069_638af581-e61c-446d-9541-1c2e2a2a493c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/12/world/12kashmir1/merlin_159180069_638af581-e