, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-12T16:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sameer Yasir and Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sameer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yasir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b05240b7-2dc1-5bcc-af6e-b10cc0918384', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b05240b7-2dc1-5bcc-af6e-b10cc0918384'}, {'abstract': 'It extracts both the seeds and juice, streamlining the process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/12/dining/pomegranate-seeds-tool.html', 'snippet': 'It extracts both the seeds and juice, streamlining the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pomegranate’s tart-sweet, jewel-like ruby seeds (arils) are a mighty challenge to extract. A new gadget from Tescoma, a company in San Martino, Italy, streamlines the usual method of holding the cut fruit in your hand over a bowl and smashing it to release the seeds. Yet even with this clever contraption, nine steps are required to force out the juice and seeds and remove the white pith. A single pomegranate will yield one-third to one-half cup of seeds and juice, which can be frozen for later use, so it pays to tackle several of them in a sitting. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ