 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Workplace Confession?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-selfcare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-work', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-13T14:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Styles Desk', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Styles Desk'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc40e97f-2e1b-5509-b1f7-b061c76b9237', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc40e97f-2e1b-5509-b1f7-b061c76b9237'}, {'abstract': 'Whether tigers or tortoises, field mice or feathered peacocks, artisanal creatures are a celebration of life itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/13/t-magazine/felt-animals.html', 'snippet': 'Whether tigers or tortoises, field mice or feathered peacocks, artisanal creatures are a celebration of life itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH EACH STAB of the needle, the fibers catch, twist and snarl. From this violence might emerge the dainty pink nose of a mouse the size of a knuckle or a Japanese waxwing’s watchful ruby eye. In these stunningly realistic animal figures, meticulously sculpted from felt, it’s the details that astound, the transformation of a material so soft and inchoate — wisps of wool shape-shifting under a maker’s fingers — into something solid, structured and anatomically precise. Far from the pillowy curves of a child’s stuffed toy, these creatures are collectible works of art that have inspired cultish (adult) adoration: An iguana meditates, its skin like fissured, parched earth; an owl tilts its head, its wings both ponderous and light; a tiger half yawns, half roars, its teeth uncannily sharp.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1239, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-felt/18tmag-felt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wonderful World of Needle-Felted Animals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handicrafts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wool and Woolen Goods', 'rank': 4, 'major': '