e an overnight. Miraculously, his father lent us his Volkswagen. My parents provided camping gear. At last the day came: Aug. 15, 1969. We were going to Woodstock. I was 16, Paul 18. It is not that we were so young, though that is true. It’s that we fell in love for the rest of our lives. Subsequent lovers told us they could sense it and broke up with us, unwilling to be second fiddles. We married in 1987, finally admitting the fire was eternal. Fifty years after Woodstock, our hearts still sing. — Chris Orr', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/07/fashion/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5/07ML-TINYLOVE-ILLO5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Love Stories: It Started at Woodstock', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-13T19:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acc2f846-6cde-5c72-bcbf-495d72e7cfc0', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acc2f846-6cde-5c72-bcbf-495d72e7cfc0'}, {'abstract': 'A family divided by immigration authorities struggles to reunite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/13/opinion/immigrant-detention-family-separation.html', 'snippet': 'A family divided by immigration authorities struggles to reunite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a hot July evening last year, I found myself in a parking lot at a detention complex in Texas. There was an outcry over the Trump administration’s policy of separating immigrant families at the border, and when I’d heard that there was a mom who needed a ride after being released, I’d volunteered to drive her. The facility was running about three hours late, and it was really hot. A security guard in a golf cart circled the perimeter of the facility. He reprimanded me for taking a photograph on my phone. I got back into my car and blasted the air-conditioning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Name Is Darlin. I Just Came Out of Detention.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Separation Policy (US Immigration)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-13T19:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Video', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Castro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d15f369-c3c0-58d5-bb03-ffa8c46694d2', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d15f369-c3c0-58d5-bb03-ffa8c46694d2'}, {'abstract': 'A Chinese-American teenager in Gilded Age Atlanta takes on a secret identity as an advice columnist in Stacey Lee’s “The Downstairs Girl.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/13/books/review/downstairs-girl-stacey-lee.html', 'snippet': 'A Chinese-American teenager in Gilded Age Atlanta takes on a secret identity as an advice columnist in Stacey Lee’s “The Downstairs Girl.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s fairly common knowledge that Chinese immigrants helped build the American railroads in the 19th century. But it’s not so widely known that Chinese laborers were shipped in by Southern plantation owners to replace emancipated slaves after the Civil War. As the number of Chinese on American soil increased, resentment against these immigrants grew proportionately, and in 1882 Congress passed the Chinese Exclusion Act under President Chester A. Arthur. It was the first American law to restrict immigration, and the only one ever to target a specific national group. It wasn’t repealed until 1943.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 906}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 678, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1356, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/13/books/review/25-BKS-KIDS2/25-BKS-KIDS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming of Age Amid a Limbo of Prejudice and Restriction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coming of Age Amid a Limbo of Prejudice and Restriction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N