Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jill P. Capuzzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jill', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Capuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58fce982-f925-5c57-bc7e-dff14b2f8b48', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58fce982-f925-5c57-bc7e-dff14b2f8b48'}, {'abstract': 'Sought after by Spike Lee, Stanley Kubrick, and Solange Knowles alike, the visual artist is changing representations of blackness in museums and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/14/t-magazine/arthur-jafa-in-bloom.html', 'snippet': 'Sought after by Spike Lee, Stanley Kubrick, and Solange Knowles alike, the visual artist is changing representations of blackness in museums and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': '“VIBES,” SAYS ARTHUR JAFA, clicking through images on a screen in his Los Angeles studio, all part of an extended mood board for a future project — photographs from the Harlem Renaissance, glamorous black-and-whites of vintage cars and fashion, work by Roy DeCarava — “more vibes.” It’s the morning after Jafa’s 58th birthday, and the polymathic artist, cinematographer and theorist of black culture threw himself a party the night before in this space in the West Adams neighborhood, not far from his home in Ladera Heights. The spotless studio is now empty save for a suite of computers and a large-scale photographic printer the size of a refrigerator. On one wall, there’s a sculpture: a seated man, his horrifically fissured back turned to the viewer. The work was inspired by an 1863 abolitionist photograph of a former slave identified as Gordon — it is at once abject and regal and, in Jafa’s 2017 rendition, creepily mesmerizing. The space is new, a place to test out ideas before placing them in a gallery, and late in the day, he shows me a prototype that didn’t work out, tucked in the back: an adult-size oblong of industrial-grade plastic. It takes a few moments of mounting dread to understand that I’m looking at the bundled shape of a lynched woman, meant to be part of a series called “Hang Time.” “Now I have a $60,000 hat stand,” he says dryly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/t-magazine/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD/18tmag-jafa-slide-YAWD-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arthur Jafa in Bloom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Gavin Brown's Enterprise", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dash, Julie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jafa, Arthur (1960- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joseph, Kahlil (1981- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kubrick, Stanley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Spike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Bradford (1977- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Eyes Wide Shut (Movie)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '4:44 (Album)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-14T09:02:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': "By Megan O'Grady", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Grady", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b10bb345-e593-5ec1-bd30-f0b1fdb62987', 'word_count': 4166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b10bb345-e593-5ec1-bd30-f0b1fdb62987'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/14/briefing/hong-kong-jeffrey-epstein-placido-domingo.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know.', 'lead_paragraph': '(Want to get this briefing by email? Here’s the sign-up.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/world/14usbriefing-amcore/merlin_159251946_485816f5-5fdf-4