ations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-14T14:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard McGregor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGregor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/94dad672-1f77-56dd-8bef-fa1be7bc84a9', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94dad672-1f77-56dd-8bef-fa1be7bc84a9'}, {'abstract': 'And make all the desserts with them: Alison Roman has five new recipes to get you started.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/14/dining/buy-all-the-fruit.html', 'snippet': 'And make all the desserts with them: Alison Roman has five new recipes to get you started.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. When Alison Roman goes to the market this time of year, she buys fruit. All of the fruit. And then she cooks it, spending more time in her kitchen making desserts than she does at any other time of the year. She has, she says, no regrets about that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/13Romanrex5-copy/13Romanrex5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/13Romanrex5-copy/13Romanrex5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/13Romanrex5-copy/13Romanrex5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/14/dining/13Romanrex5-copy/13Romanrex5-superJum