es.com/2019/08/15/opinion/italy-alcohol.html', 'snippet': 'A new generation has rediscovered the social charms of imbibing an aperitif before dinner, turning Italy this summer into one vast bar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — My youth was aperitif-free. It was the 1970s and we concentrated on discos, warm beer on the beach, pizza, sleepless nights with friends and a bottle — or more — of cheap wine. We weren’t fussy. Aperitivi — a ritual pre-dinner drink to begin the evening’s imbibing — was for old people: my parents, uncles and aunts, and on holidays, mostly. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/merlin_39066745_66fccbc3-0949-4703-bcd9-9f824db9f7c1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/merlin_39066745_66fccbc3-0949-4703-bcd9-9f824db9f7c1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/merlin_39066745_66fccbc3-0949-4703-bcd9-9f824db9f7c1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/merlin_39066745_66fccbc3-0949-4703-bcd9-9f824db9f7c1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/00Severgnini-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/00Severgnini-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/12/opinion/00Severgnini/00Severgnini-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alla Salute! Italy’s Aperitivo Is Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennial Generation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prosecco (Wine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salvini, Matteo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soldati, Mario', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lombardy (Italy)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-15T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beppe Severgnini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beppe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severgnini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/82426d91-e366-51a0-a425-dcf976d67c21', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82426d91-e366-51a0-a425-dcf976d67c21'}, {'abstract': 'And she’s playing to win.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/15/opinion/stacey-abrams-elections.html', 'snippet': 'And she’s playing to win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everywhere she goes, Stacey Abrams is treated like a rock star — or a presidential candidate. I and all my friends wanted her to jump into the presidential race. Instead, she’s doing something more important. She’s creating an apparatus to fight voter suppression across the country, a prize that’s essential to a fair and functioning democracy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/15/opinion/15price-web/15price-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/15/opinion/15price-web/15price-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/15/opinion/15price-web/15price-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/15/opinion/15price-web/15price-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/15/opinion/15price-web/15price-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/15/opinion/15price-web/15price-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/0