tial government document containing evidence so critical it had the potential to change the course of an American tragedy was kept in the dark for more than a decade. The document, known as a “prosecution memo,” details how government lawyers believed that Purdue Pharma, the maker of the powerful opioid, OxyContin, knew early on that the drug was fueling a rise in abuse and addiction. They also gathered evidence indicating that the company’s executives had misled the public and Congress. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Secret Opioid Memo That Could Have Slowed an Epidemic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'OxyContin (Drug)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sackler Family', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Purdue Pharma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sackler, Richard (1945- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Weekly (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hulu.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-16T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Universal', 'section_name': 'The Weekly', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce0a83c7-4165-5c1f-ab75-9b8bcaadef9e', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce0a83c7-4165-5c1f-ab75-9b8bcaadef9e'}, {'abstract': 'One of the Upcountry city’s most intriguing areas is West Greenville, an enclave that has been transformed into an artistic and entrepreneurial district.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/16/travel/five-places-to-visit-in-greenville-sc.html', 'snippet': 'One of the Upcountry city’s most intriguing areas is West Greenville, an enclave that has been transformed into an artistic and entrepreneurial district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greenville, S.C., near the Blue Ridge Mountains, has emerged as a buzzy destination for the culinary and creative arts after years of  economic growth and urban revitalization. One of the Upcountry city’s most intriguing areas is West Greenville, the former hub of the city’s textile production. In recent years, the enclave known as “The Village” of West Greenville has been transformed into an artistic and entrepreneurial district with an eclectic mix of small businesses. There’s a James Beard-semifinalist restaurant, a host of independent galleries, as well as the Greenville Center for Creative Arts, which houses an art school and regularly holds public events and workshops.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/16/travel/16Greenville-5Places6/merlin_158731833_1a2b3564-6b84-4f19-ad14-7fc6fb3e139a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/16/travel/16Greenville-5Places6/merlin_158731833_1a2b3564-6b84-4f19-ad14-7fc6fb3e139a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/16/travel/16Greenville-5Places6/merlin_158731833_1a2b3564-6b84-4f19-ad14-7fc6fb3e139a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/16/travel/16Greenville-5Places6/merlin_158731833_1a2b3564-6b84-4f19-ad14-7fc6fb3e139a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo'