youngsters these days, an hour of free play is like a drop of water in the desert. Of course they’re miserable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to the psychologist Peter Gray, children today are more depressed than they were during the Great Depression and more anxious than they were at the height of the Cold War. A 2019 study published in the Journal of Abnormal Psychology found that between 2009 and 2017, rates of depression rose by more than 60 percent among those ages 14 to 17, and 47 percent among those ages 12 to 13. This isn’t just a matter of increased diagnoses. The number of children and teenagers who were seen in emergency rooms with suicidal thoughts or having attempted suicide doubled between 2007 and 2015.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1018, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2035, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18brooks/18brooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Have Ruined Childhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Have Ruined Childhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-17T18:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa66008-4e53-56b5-bacd-5b5bd2309d58', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa66008-4e53-56b5-bacd-5b5bd2309d58'}, {'abstract': 'With the loss of the two award-winning publications, digital media got a little less brainy in the summer of ’19.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/17/business/media/pacific-standard-topic-magazines.html', 'snippet': 'With the loss of the two award-winning publications, digital media got a little less brainy in the summer of ’19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pacific Standard and Topic, a pair of award-winning publications that stood out from the pack of click-hungry websites, were founded by rich patrons. The generosity of their benefactors allowed them to publish robust journalism at a time when old-line magazine publishers like Time Inc. were being sold for parts — but it wasn’t enough to keep them from folding. Both died this summer, when their backers decided they were no longer worth the expense.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/11/business/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01/11PACIFICSTANDARD-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Closing of Pacific Standard and Topic Shows Perils of Depending on a Rich Patron', 'kicker': 'Media Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defunct Publications Show Even a Wealthy Patron Isn’t a Sure Bet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Standard (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Topic (Magazine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sage Publications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'First Look Media Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-17T18:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7559897e-9594-597e-a249-650e5a7ddad4', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7559897e-9594-597e-a249-650e5a7ddad4'}, {'abstract': 'There are better ways of doing social justice work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/17/opinion/sunday/cancel-culture-call-out.html', 'snippet': 'There are better ways of doing social justice work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s call-out culture is so seductive, I often have to resist the overwhelming temptation to clap back at people on social media who get on my nerves. Call-outs happen when people publicly shame each other online, at the office, in classrooms or anywhere humans have beef with one another. But I believe there are better ways of doing social justice work.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18ross/18ross-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m a Black Feminist. I Think Call-Out Culture Is Toxic.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Call-Out Culture Is Toxic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-17T18:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Loretta Ross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Loretta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/01c26e11-efb9-5775-9be2-3a84a9c7c877', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01c26e11-efb9-5775-9be2-3a84a9c7c877'}, {'abstract': 'This is not 1989 and Hong Kong is not Beijing, yet unarmed students are again in danger of repression by the Chinese military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/17/opinion/sunday/hong-kong-china.html', 'snippet': 'This is not 1989 and Hong Kong is not Beijing, yet unarmed students are again in danger of repression by the Chinese military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty years ago, on May 19, 1989, Zhao Ziyang, general secretary of the Chinese Communist Party, stood in Tiananmen Square. It was 5 in the morning and Zhao, exhausted, holding a loudspeaker, addressed student demonstrators, thousands of whom were on Day 7 of a hunger strike. “Students, we came too late,” he said. “I am sorry.  Sorry. Whatever you say and criticize about us is deserved.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18Thiem2/merlin_159261282_b3b03ec1-538d-4e81-89c2-3d3b1aeebbf6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/18/opinion/sunday/18Thiem2/merlin_159261282_b3b03ec1-538d-4e81-89c2-3d3b1aeebbf6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {