[], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Is a New Recession Imminent? Here’s How One Could Happen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-08-18T04:34:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fed2127-9f4e-52bc-a808-c91a688f90e4', 'word_count': 47, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fed2127-9f4e-52bc-a808-c91a688f90e4'}, {'abstract': 'The season finale of the Boston drama airs on Showtime, and F.B.I. agents investigate more sinister killers in the second season of “Mindhunter” on Netflix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/18/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday-city-on-a-hill-and-mindhunter.html', 'snippet': 'The season finale of the Boston drama airs on Showtime, and F.B.I. agents investigate more sinister killers in the second season of “Mindhunter” on Netflix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CITY ON A HILL 9 p.m. on Showtime. A slew of heavyweight actors and the robust backdrop of Boston have shaped an ambitious first season for “City on a Hill,” which is airing its finale tonight. The drama follows Decourcy Ward (Aldis Hodge), an assistant district attorney, and Jackie Rohr (Kevin Bacon), a veteran F.B.I. agent, as they each find their own way to navigate the city’s criminal justice system, which is rife with corruption. Mike Hale writes in a review for The New York Times that the show “keeps threatening to be interesting and exciting, but so far it hasn’t pulled off the job.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/18/arts/18tvcol-cityonahill/merlin_159301902_78229a81-d3aa-4310-93c4-0ad429fed1a8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width