er took away even that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — One minute, it was a wedding — nearly a thousand guests packed under one roof, a thin partition segregating them by gender. Men shimmied to a live band, women spun to a D.J. Their invitation cards read: We celebrate “with a world of hope and desire.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Minute It Was an Afghan Wedding. The Next, a Funeral for 63.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Afghans Felt Safe, Bomb Wreaks Carnage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-18T19:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mujib Mashal, Fatima Faizi and Fahim Abed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mujib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fatima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Faizi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Fahim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9731f86c-5