cc44d36a16d7'}, {'abstract': 'Their bipartisan effort comes after a smaller group of the state representatives met last month with antitrust officials at the Justice Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/19/technology/state-ag-tech-investigations.html', 'snippet': 'Their bipartisan effort comes after a smaller group of the state representatives met last month with antitrust officials at the Justice Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state attorneys general in more than a dozen states are preparing to begin an antitrust investigation of the tech giants, according to two people briefed on the discussions, increasing pressure on the companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/merlin_158035872_a3654d98-3ab3-4435-9e08-d86c49ba9ed2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/merlin_158035872_a3654d98-3ab3-4435-9e08-d86c49ba9ed2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/merlin_158035872_a3654d98-3ab3-4435-9e08-d86c49ba9ed2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/merlin_158035872_a3654d98-3ab3-4435-9e08-d86c49ba9ed2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/19BIGTECH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/19BIGTECH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19BIGTECH/19BIGTECH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'State Attorneys General Said to Be Near Formal Investigation of Tech Companies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'States Are Said To Plan Inquiry Of Tech Giants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-19T23:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d223a241-862c-5593-9f44-a21b9d9b500b', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d223a241-862c-5593-9f44-a21b9d9b500b'}, {'abstract': 'After making baseless claims of voter fraud, the president has turned to a new way of explaining his loss of the popular vote in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/19/us/politics/google-votes-election-trump.html', 'snippet': 'After making baseless claims of voter fraud, the president has turned to a new way of explaining his loss of the popular vote in 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. Trump lost the popular vote by almost 2.9 million in the 2016 election and has long attributed this loss to baseless claims of voter fraud. Now Mr. Trump suggests that he would have lost the popular vote by a much smaller margin, or even won it, were it not for Google’s machinations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fact-Checking Trump’s Claim That Google ‘Manipulated’ Millions of Votes for Clinton', 'kicker': 'Fact Check', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-19T23:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Qiu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qiu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3300c40e-e348-510a-bddb-c3a72b9a9421', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3300c40e-e348-510a-bddb-c3a72b9a9421'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s resolve to take significant action appears to have softened, and he has reverted to reiterating conservative positions on guns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/19/us/politics/trump-gun-laws.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s resolve to take significant action appears to have softened, and he has reverted to reiterating conservative positions on guns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Days after a pair of deadly mass shootings in Texas and Ohio, President Trump said he was prepared to endorse what he described as “very meaningful background checks” that would be possible because of his “greater influence now over the Senate and over the House.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/us/politics/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/19/us/politics/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/us/politics/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/us/politics/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/us/politics/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO/19dc-trumpguns2-PROMO-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbna