', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82b811e0-5dfb-5316-8440-d1c69ae1d7ad', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82b811e0-5dfb-5316-8440-d1c69ae1d7ad'}, {'abstract': 'On Facebook and Reddit, retail-focused groups remember the heyday of malls and share stories of shuttered department stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/21/style/retail-facebook-groups-reddit.html', 'snippet': 'On Facebook and Reddit, retail-focused groups remember the heyday of malls and share stories of shuttered department stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Changes in retail spaces — say, new cash registers at the nearest big-box store — are met by most shoppers with a “huh,” if anything. But for some, even the most seemingly minor tweaks are noticed and documented online as part of modern American history.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/fashion/16retailgroups-mall-1960s/16retailgroups-mall-1960s-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/22/fashion/16retailgroups-mall-1960s/16retailgroups-mall-1960s-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/fashion/16retailgroups-mall-1960s/16retailgroups-mall-1960s-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/fashion/16retailgroups-mall-1960s/16retail