have to gather as much support as possible both at home and abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — From a distance, our political story this year seems simple: Good pro-market guy loses, bad guy wins and populism comes back. It is not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/merlin_159152982_c69faf0a-83a9-4139-9a5b-b57266380a02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/merlin_159152982_c69faf0a-83a9-4139-9a5b-b57266380a02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/merlin_159152982_c69faf0a-83a9-4139-9a5b-b57266380a02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/merlin_159152982_c69faf0a-83a9-4139-9a5b-b57266380a02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/21Garcia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/21Garcia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/21/opinion/21Garcia1/21Garcia1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina’s Likely Nex