', '_id': 'nyt://article/05324b36-efa9-5624-bd32-b49ab8ded4c9', 'word_count': 1311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05324b36-efa9-5624-bd32-b49ab8ded4c9'}, {'abstract': 'A lively reggae soundtrack and a Jamaican setting: It’s not “The Harder They Come” but Perry Henzell’s long-lost follow-up to it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/movies/no-place-like-home-review.html', 'snippet': 'A lively reggae soundtrack and a Jamaican setting: It’s not “The Harder They Come” but Perry Henzell’s long-lost follow-up to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1973 Jamaican movie “The Harder They Come” was a hybrid crime drama and musical with an irresistible premise: a singer hits the top of the pop charts at the same time he hits the top of the most-wanted list. Starring the reggae stalwart Jimmy Cliff, the movie was directed by Perry Henzell; Chris Blackwell, whose Island Records was instrumental in introducing reggae to the United States and Britain, was a producer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/arts/23NOPLACE/23NOPLACE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/23/arts/23NOPLACE/23NOPLACE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/arts/23NOPLACE/23NOPLACE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/arts/23NOPLACE/23NOPLACE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2022, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url