5, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b4edceb-69e0-5fe1-bd3c-144b4072e598'}, {'abstract': 'Both sides agreed to move on years after Mr. Kimball started Milk Street, a similar cooking and media venture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/dining/christopher-kimball-americas-test-kitchen-lawsuit.html', 'snippet': 'Both sides agreed to move on years after Mr. Kimball started Milk Street, a similar cooking and media venture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long legal battle between America’s Test Kitchen and Christopher Kimball, the company’s founder who left and started a similar cooking and media enterprise called Christopher Kimball’s Milk Street, is over.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 539}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 920, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1423, 'width': 1584, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/23/dining/22Milkstreet-print/22Milkstreet1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christopher Kimball and America’s Test Kitchen Settle Lawsuit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dueling Cooking Franchises Drop Their Knives to Settle a Long Legal Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "America's Test Kitchen LLC", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milk Street Kitchen (CPK Media LLC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimball, Christopher', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-22T18:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca6c7239-060e-5ae4-92fe-95790de2f478', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca6c7239-060e-5ae4-92fe-95790de2f478'}, {'abstract': 'The scheme, cooked up by 4chan trolls, sought to stoke Jewish infighting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/opinion/technology/white-supremacists-4chan-trolls-jews.html', 'snippet': 'The scheme, cooked up by 4chan trolls, sought to stoke Jewish infighting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband and I were sitting on a tarmac at Newark Airport, just having landed from a vacation in France, relieved to come home, where we could be openly Jewish again. Visits to that country are always laced with stress for us, Orthodox Jews whose appearance broadcasts our identity. Being home meant that my husband, a rabbi, didn’t have to hide his kipa or tuck in his tzitzis. It meant we no longer had to check emergency exit signs in kosher restaurants, or change the subject when cabdrivers asked us where we’re from.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 602}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2041, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22Goldschmidt-Sub/22Goldschmidt-Sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'White Supremacists Stole My Rabbi Husband’s Identity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bigots Try to Stoke Jewish Infighting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Theft', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '4chan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-22T18:59:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Opinion | Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Avital Chizhik-Goldschmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Avital', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chizhik-Goldschmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/90fc4e60-3eb4-5b24-9efa-b1bd21b45c86', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90fc4e60-3eb4-5b24-9efa-b1bd21b45c86'}, {'abstract': 'As media monoliths bundle their offerings, consumers will once again have to pay for a bunch of shows they don’t want.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/opinion/netflix-hulu-cable.html', 'snippet': 'As media monoliths bundle their offerings, consumers will once again have to pay for a bunch of shows they don’t want.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By 2010, nine in 10 American homes were subscribed to a pay-television service. M