94e-8331-98041ae6711f'}, {'abstract': 'This teaching guide, the second in our seven-unit writing curriculum, includes daily writing prompts, lessons based on selected mentor texts, and the announcement of a new personal narrative essay contest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/learning/personal-narrative-writing-unit.html', 'snippet': 'This teaching guide, the second in our seven-unit writing curriculum, includes daily writing prompts, lessons based on selected mentor texts, and the announcement of a new personal narrative essay contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to our second writing unit of the school year. Below you’ll find a detailed description of each element, as well as ways to put them together to make your own custom writing unit. To learn more about other writing units, visit our writing curriculum overview. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 611}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/24/learning/StoryCoasterLN/StoryCoasterLN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unit 2: Teach Narrative Writing With The New York Times', 'kicker': 'Writing Curriculum', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-22T20:52:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0816be1b-4434-59af-a627-5998d1339543', 'word_count': 1408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0816be1b-4434-59af-a627-5998d1339543'}, {'abstract': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/books/review/10-new-books-we-recommend-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deep history echoes through this week’s list of recommended books. Téa Obreht sets her second novel, “Inland” — which follows the widely acclaimed “The Tiger’s Wife” (2011) — in the American West of the 19th century. Rudyard Kipling first visited the United States in 1889, and Christopher Benfey’s “If” argues that his engagement with this country made him the writer he became. Julia Blackburn’s “Time Song” goes way, way back to envision a part of the world as it was 8,000 years ago. The latest book by the Nobel laureate Svetlana Alexievich translated into English captures the memories of Russian children who lived through World War II, and Ludmila Ulitskaya’s novel “Jacob’s Ladder” unfurls against more than a century of Russian history. And in “Bagehot,” we’re given the portrait of a multitalented British Victorian who deserves to be better known.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 2041, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/books/25edchoice/25edchoice-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'su