'By Sarah Vowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bc95126-dbc0-54ce-b446-07869207d13c', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bc95126-dbc0-54ce-b446-07869207d13c'}, {'abstract': 'Are Democrats hexing the Trump boom with bad thoughts?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/opinion/trump-payroll-tax-cut.html', 'snippet': 'Are Democrats hexing the Trump boom with bad thoughts?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost four decades ago then-candidate George H.W. Bush used the phrase “voodoo economic policy” to describe Ronald Reagan’s claim that cutting taxes for the rich would pay for itself. He was more prescient than he could have imagined.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22krugman/22krugman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22krugman/22krugman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22krugman/22krugman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22krugman/22krugman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/22/opinion/22krugman/22krugman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'