ursday struggled to contain growing global outrage over its environmental policies, which have paved the way for runaway deforestation of the world’s largest rain forest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Amazon Rain Forest Ablaze, Brazil Faces Global Backlash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Scorched Amazon Smolders, Brazil Fights Against Global Outrage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON RIVER BASIN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON JUNGLE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolsonaro, Jair (1955- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous People', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-22T23:06:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manuela Andreoni, Letícia Casado and Ernesto Londoño', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manuela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andreoni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Letícia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lo