t', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creator of R&amp;B Music  That Defies Labels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'RHYTHM AND BLUES (MUSIC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fae, Dizzy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-23T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Hawgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59158544-714b-5b8d-bc29-95f71c9557a8', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59158544-714b-5b8d-bc29-95f71c9557a8'}, {'abstract': 'Here are some names to seek out on the outside courts at the U.S.T.A. National Tennis Center during the first week of the tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/23/sports/tennis/us-open-players-to-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Here are some names to seek out on the outside courts at the U.S.T.A. National Tennis Center during the first week of the tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, Andreescu, 19, became the first Canadian woman in the Open era to win the Rogers Cup in Toronto. It was her first tournament since withdrawing from the French Open with a shoulder injury. Andreescu won four consecutive three-set matches on her way to the title in Toronto, where she won when Serena Williams retired during the final because of back spasms. In March, Andreescu surprised the tennis world by winning at Indian Wells, Calif., defeating Angelique Kerber to claim her first tour title. Andreescu, No. 15 in the world, has credited her speedy rise in the rankings to the meditation and visualization techniques her mother taught her when she was 12. With her unflappable demeanor, Andreescu is rock solid from the baseline, with superb movement and disciplined shot selection. She uses the drop shot shrewdly, often wrong-footing opponents by going behind them. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/merlin_159163158_5bca83d9-46a4-4bd8-8a3c-c884a9a11b99-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/merlin_159163158_5bca83d9-46a4-4bd8-8a3c-c884a9a11b99-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/merlin_159163158_5bca83d9-46a4-4bd8-8a3c-c884a9a11b99-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/merlin_159163158_5bca83d9-46a4-4bd8-8a3c-c884a9a11b99-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/23open-players2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/23open-players2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/26/sports/23open-players1-print/23open-players2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2019 U.S. Ope