lead_paragraph': 'PUNS AND ANAGRAMS  — We know Andrew J. Reis well for his wide-ranging, congenial crossword puzzles; this is his third “Panda” and another admirable feather in his cap. There is a lot of personality in this particular variety of variety puzzle, I think. The incomparable Mel Taub was wholly responsible for them for many years, and now that we are seeing different constructors we are seeing some different flourishes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Puns and Anagrams', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-08-24T15:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/721f4189-289a-5f2b-abfd-57cf05ff28dc', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/721f4189-289a-5f2b-abfd-57cf05ff28dc'}, {'abstract': 'Readers react with both support and skepticism to a Business Roundtable statement about caring for more than shareholder interests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/24/opinion/letters/corporations-social-responsibility-business-roundtable.html', 'snippet': 'Readers react with both support and skepticism to a Business Roundtable statement about caring for more than shareholder interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19ROUNDTABLE-COMBO/19ROUNDTABLE-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/19/business/19ROUNDTABLE-COMBO/19ROUNDTABLE-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 's