er died from a heart attack. Mr. Colbert also was 10 when his father died in a plane crash that also took two of his brothers’ lives. Their early losses, both men agreed, shaped their priorities, their worldviews and the adults they ultimately became.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25edelman/25edelman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Couldn’t Say ‘My Mother’ Without Crying', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Quick Fix for Childhood Grief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Anderson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-25T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Edelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/92103506-6c3c-5d92-8903-ac1626deefb1', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92103506-6c3c-5d92-8903-ac1626deefb1'}, {'abstract': 'Why do the president and many of his opponents act as though American political life is just another film noir?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/25/opinion/trump-warren-sanders-corruption.html', 'snippet': 'Why do the president and many of his opponents act as though American political life is just another film noir?', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump wants his supporters to know that he is still draining the swamp over which he has presided for nearly three years. One of his Democratic rivals, Senator Elizabeth Warren, says Americans are trapped in a “rigged system that props up the rich and powerful and kicks dirt on everyone else.” Her colleague and fellow candidate, Senator Bernie Sanders, calls it “a corrupt political system designed to protect the wealthy and the powerful.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/25/opinion/25weiner/25weiner-articleLarg