able', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Manufacturers', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Retail Federation', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolten, Joshua B', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mnuchin, Steven T', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-25T23:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/252b4abc-3e6b-54b8-b8e3-dfb98095b545', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/252b4abc-3e6b-54b8-b8e3-dfb98095b545'}, {'abstract': 'A fireball producer is giving him a comeback chance while also trying to revive the tired celebrity news genre. It’s Mr. Bush’s first TV job since the infamous “Access Hollywood” tape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/25/business/media/billy-bush-extraextra.html', 'snippet': 'A fireball producer is giving him a comeback chance while also trying to revive the tired celebrity news genre. It’s Mr. Bush’s first TV job since the infamous “Access Hollywood” tape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BURBANK, Calif. — The television producer Lisa Gregorisch-Dempsey is known for her terrifying candor. The nameplate on her desk at Telepictures, where she has run the celebrity news show “Extra” for 19 years, sums up her style: “I’ll be nicer if you’ll be smarter.” But even her longtime lieutenants were a bit startled by the way she laid it on the line for Billy Bush when she interviewed him for a job last year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{