', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/48a3283e-eeb7-5df0-9ff3-a9a6f2b8727a', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48a3283e-eeb7-5df0-9ff3-a9a6f2b8727a'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to throw out a freeloading stepdaughter and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/27/magazine/my-layabout-stepdaughter-and-her-boyfriend-live-with-me-can-i-kick-them-out.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to throw out a freeloading stepdaughter and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is my ethical responsibility toward the two 20-year-olds living at home with me? One is my stepdaughter; one is her boyfriend (whom we took in a few years ago because his parents are both addicts). Neither goes to school; neither works, except for an occasional babysitting gig. They do little around the house to help. I pay all their bills and have provided a car for them to use (presumably to get to and from work/school, although neither is happening). When is enough enough? Name Withheld', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge-v36.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge-v36.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-jumbo-v36.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-superJumbo-v36.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard-v37.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard-v37.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/01mag-ethicist-imageNEW/01mag-ethicist-image1-thumbLarge-v37.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Layabout Stepdaughter and Her Boyfriend Live With Me. Can I Kick Them Out?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Layabout Stepdaughter And Her Boyfriend Live With Me. Can I Kick Them Out?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-27T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7252cad-6ae4-5637-84a5-62e5a75e2575', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7252cad-6ae4-5637-84a5-62e5a75e2575'}, {'abstract': 'Get to know coworkers in person or through encrypted messenger apps. Crowdsource specific demands. Stage the event in the morning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/27/magazine/how-to-organize-a-walkout.html', 'snippet': 'Get to know coworkers in person or through encrypted messenger apps. Crowdsource specific demands. Stage the event in the morning.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You need to create connections with your co-workers,” says Meredith Whittaker, a lead organizer of the November protest in which some 20,000 Google employees walked out of offices around the world. Know your colleagues; build trust; get together to articulate common concerns and a shared vision of change. Avoid detection by doing these things in person or over encrypted messenger apps like Signal. Organizing a robust worker movement can take years. “It’s like building muscle,” Whittaker says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 607}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1012, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01Mag-Tip-1/01Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Organize a Walkout', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Organize A Walkout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wayfair Inc.', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'WHITTAKER, MEREDITH', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-27T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8114e676-5af0-5f6b-8955-83bbd8477a86', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8114e676-5af0-5f6b-8955-83bbd8477a86'}, {'abstract': 'In the last presidential election, the idea of abolishing private health insurance was confined to the far left of American politics. Now it’s the central argument of the Democratic primary race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/27/magazine/medicare-for-all-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'In the last presidential election, the idea of abolishing private health insurance was confined to the far left of American politics. Now it’s the central argument of the Democratic primary race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 17, 2016, 15 prominent Democratic Party activists and elected officials gathered in a hotel conference room in downtown Phoenix. Their job was to formulate language for the party platform, which would be adopted at the following month’s national convention in Philadelphia. But the platform-drafting committee also had an unspoken mission: to defuse the lingering intraparty tension in the wake of Bernie Sanders’s spirited but unsuccessful primary battle against Hillary Clinton.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '41', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/magazine/01mag-meadicare-01/01mag-meadicare-01-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How ‘Medicare for All’ Went Mainstream', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All or Nothing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Nurses United', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-27T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Draper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df1ce3b8-de48-5544-bd70-440811df8827', 'word_count': 6361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1ce3b8-de48-5544-bd70-440811df8827'}, {'abstract': 'In “Pumpkinheads,” two work pals navigate the fine line between friendship and love. It’s set in a pumpkin patch, with dreamy art by Faith Erin Hicks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/27/books/review/pumpkinheads-rainbow-rowell-faith-erin-hicks.html', 'snippet': 'In “Pumpkinheads,” two work pals navigate the fine line between friendship and love. It’s set in a pumpkin patch, with dreamy art by Faith Erin Hicks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think back on the most amazing pumpkin patch you’ve ever been to, then add some fall-inspired snack booths: a Pumpkin Bomb Stand, a S’mores Pit, a Freeto Pie Stop and Pappy’s Apples. This is the appealing setting of PUMPKINHEADS (First Second, 224 pp., $17.99; ages 12 and up), Rainbow Rowell’s first graphic novel, with art by Faith Erin Hicks. Rowell’s other young adult books, like the best-selling “Eleanor & Park,” typically lean toward darker themes and misfit characters. But this story of two friends working their last shift together is lighter, more buoyant.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Glaser/01Glaser-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Glaser/01Glaser-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Glaser/01Glaser-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Glaser/01Glaser-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Glaser/01Glaser-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Glaser/01Gla