entury skill. In this 54-minute webinar, recorded live in March 2019, join educators from The Learning Network, the American Statistical Association and Desmos, as well as guest teachers and students, as we discuss ways to teach and learn with the award-winning graphics from The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-articleLarge.png', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-jumbo.png', 'height': 479, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-superJumbo.png', 'height': 500, 'width': 1070, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/learning/TobaccoGraph/TobaccoGraph-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On-Demand Webinar: Teach With Graphs From The New York Times', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-08-27T15:20:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f67fb808-cc96-556f-8b16-d5c40a6428d9', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f67fb808-cc96-556f-8b16-d5c40a6428d9'}, {'abstract': 'In a city running over with hot pots, Da Long Yi, a new restaurant on Canal Street, has special appeal for those wary of heat or too many choices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/27/dining/da-long-yi-hot-pot-review-pete-wells.html', 'snippet': 'In a city running over with hot pots, Da Long Yi, a new restaurant on Canal Street, has special appeal for those wary of heat or too many choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is getting crowded with hot pots. The city is not yet in the same league as, say, Chongqing, where the dish is said to have originated and where an association dedicated to keeping track of such things says there are about 50,000 places to eat it. New York, by my count, has a mere two or three dozen, most of them in the sections of Brooklyn, Queens and Lower Manhattan that have considerable Chinese populations. But new hot pot restaurants seem to arrive every few weeks, with some independent operators among a growing number of chains from China.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/27/dining/27REST-DAL-slide-N2XY/27REST-DAL-slide-N2XY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/27/dining/27REST-DAL-slide-N2XY/27REST-DAL-slide-N2XY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'