ke his modernist forebears, counts pounds. He calls one coming exhibition his “heaviest show ever.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do we talk about when we talk about sculpture? Not pounds or kilograms, for sure. It hardly deepens our view of Giacometti’s spindly figures or Calder’s light-as-air mobiles, or even the pioneering brown-hued “Guitar” that Picasso assembled from sheet metal, to know they weigh, say, 50 or 60 or 100 pounds.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/arts/01serra1/01serra1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard Serra Is Carrying the Weight of the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Richard Serra Is Still The Man of Steel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serra, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Forged Rounds (Exhibit)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-28T09:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22594ddd-221f-54b4-bdad-7dbd2c5543a1', 'word_count': 2526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22594ddd-221f-54b4-bdad-7dbd2c5543a1'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s Alentejo region has the last unspoiled stretch of Atlantic coast in all of southern Europe, with 40 miles of nearly untouched beaches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/28/travel/portugal-alentejo-melides-atlantic-coast-beaches-villages.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s Alentejo region has the last unspoiled stretch of Atlantic coast in all of southern Europe, with 40 miles of nearly untouched beaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The local butcher, with his daughter standing by his side, was selling roasted whole chickens and slabs of fresh-cut beef to customers who only had to look into the store and nod to put in their orders, much as it has been done in this tiny hillside village in rural Portugal for decades now. Routines here are as well-worn as the cobblestone streets.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd-4903-a61c-3ef6da1ff839-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd-4903-a61c-3ef6da1ff839-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd-4903-a61c-3ef6da1ff839-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd-4903-a61c-3ef6da1ff839-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd-4903-a61c-3ef6da1ff839-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd-4903-a61c-3ef6da1ff839-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28Portugal-Melides4/merlin_158862714_499a04c0-f5bd