middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saval', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5453ccfa-b1f3-5421-b734-05473936e340', 'word_count': 3858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5453ccfa-b1f3-5421-b734-05473936e340'}, {'abstract': 'He transformed a fading Welsh town into a tourist magnet by buying books in bulk from colleges, libraries, defunct wholesalers and collectors’ estates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/28/books/richard-booth-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He transformed a fading Welsh town into a tourist magnet by buying books in bulk from colleges, libraries, defunct wholesalers and collectors’ estates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Booth, who collected a million titles to transform a fading 12th-century Welsh market town into a mecca for secondhand book fanciers, and who celebrated his improbable success one April Fools’ Day by crowning himself with a title he concocted — “King Richard Coeur de Livre” — died on Aug. 20 in Cusop, Wales. He was 80.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/obituaries/29SUBbooth-print1/merlin_159752055_bfeb5eee-5c2d-4efe-bf8e-da94d0fdba7b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/29/obituaries/29SUBbooth-print1/merlin_159752055_bfeb5eee-5c2d-4efe-bf8e-da94d0fdba7b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/obituaries/29SUBbooth-print1/merlin_159752055_bfeb5eee-5c2d-4efe-bf8e-da94d0fdba7b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'