ppets of sounds into intricate songs about a host of anxieties.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I can hear, I can hear crying,” Justin Vernon repeats, louder and louder, as music rises around him: drums, guitars and horns along with voices mixed to sound near and far. It’s a track called “Naeem” that arrives at the midpoint of “i,i,” the fourth album Vernon has made as Bon Iver, and like most of his songs it’s a bundle of disparate emotions and connotations. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/arts/28album-boniver2/merlin_159831483_1e211524-9c8d-45ce-bc3a-cb0c65d4549c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/29/arts/28album-boniver2/merlin_159831483_1e211524-9c8d-45ce-bc3a-cb0c65d4549c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/arts/28album-boniver2/merlin_159831483_1e211524-9c8d-45ce-bc3a-cb0c65d4549c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/arts/28album-boniver2/merlin_159831483_1e211524-9c8d-45ce-bc3a-cb0c65d4549c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1178, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/arts/28album-boniver2/28album-boniver2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/29/arts/28album-boniver2/28album-boniver2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'