 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Loewe SA', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Noten, Dries', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jil Sander AG', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-28T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clara Balzary and Sasha Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Balzary', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bcfd0f6-b941-5231-b502-115d365e6343', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bcfd0f6-b941-5231-b502-115d365e6343'}, {'abstract': 'To control shine, inflammation and other climate-related concerns, look to gently efficient solutions that work with skin — not against it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/28/t-magazine/summer-skin-care.html', 'snippet': 'To control shine, inflammation and other climate-related concerns, look to gently efficient solutions that work with skin — not against it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer, for all its pleasures, can send skin into a state of chaos. Heat and humidity can unleash inflammation, oil and redness while generous applications of sunscreen can form a dulling residue over time. At her Manhattan practice, the dermatologist Dr. Macrene Alexiades-Armenakas finds that the summer months have “a profound effect” on skin. Similarly, the Brooklyn facialist Crystal Greene says her clients’ skin often goes haywire in July and August, when she sees a rise in “breakouts, dehydration and hyperpigmentation.” A purifying routine can bring relief, say the experts, but resist the urge to cleanse too deeply — obliterating all traces of oil or reaching for super-potent astringents can strip your complexion and leave it in worse condition. “Skin has a natural barrier that is lightly acidic to protect us from invaders, like bacteria and allergens, which can cause irritation,” says Greene. “So any products need to support that barrier.” Here, a four-step cleansing ritual that respects — and balances — compromised skin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/05/t-magazine/2tmag-beauty-01/2tmag-beauty-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 