'nyt://article/445e6dbb-9c31-5eae-9616-599ff1c4beaf'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin McDonald, once part of the Canadian comedy troupe, plays for audience nostalgia in ‘Kevin McDonald: Alive on 42nd Street.’', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/28/theater/review-kevin-mcdonald-kids-in-the-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin McDonald, once part of the Canadian comedy troupe, plays for audience nostalgia in ‘Kevin McDonald: Alive on 42nd Street.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are tough houses, there are friendly houses and there are houses so freakishly primed for laughter that they actively guffaw at the turn-off-your-cellphone message. This was the house that greeted Kevin McDonald at the second performance of “Kevin McDonald: Alive on 42nd Street,” a solo show with what we’ll generously call music.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 957, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 957}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 642, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1434, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/arts/28kevinmcdonald/merlin_159805695_192be19d-3edd-40e3-ba82-4df4ed3c4277-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Kids in the Hall,’ Rehashed for Adults in a Theater', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Kids in the Hall’ Rehashed For Adults in a Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Kevin (1961- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kids in the Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Kevin McDonald: Alive on 42nd Street (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-28T18:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/33b847ce-aefa-5403-907c-364e5b096c4e', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33b847ce-aefa-5403-907c-364e5b096c4e'}, {'abstract': 'They’re right about ethics and the environment. If you won’t join them, at least respect their effort to build a sustainable future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/28/opinion/vegan-food.html', 'snippet': 'They’re right about ethics and the environment. If you won’t join them, at least respect their effort to build a sustainable future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Popeyes’ new fried chicken sandwich went viral for its deliciousness last week, I did not pause, not even for a second, to consider the vast toll of suffering and environmental destruction inherent in its rise. I am guessing you didn’t either; indeed, I can already feel your eyes rolling deep into your head at the mere suggestion that there’s anything to feel guilty about regarding the sold-out sandwich. So before we go on, let me warn you: The rest of this column is going to give your eye-rolling muscles a very good workout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/opinion/28manjoo-web/28manjoo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/28/opinion/28manjoo-web/28manjoo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/opinion/28manjoo-web/28manjoo-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/opinion/28manjoo-web/28manjoo-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/28/opinion/28manjoo-web/28manjoo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/28/opinion/28manjoo-web/28manjoo-we