the strange and sometimes alluring: Siberia, with its warbling throat singers, as well as a potato farm in Maine and the phenomenon known as A.S.M.R.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/29/arts/design/mika-rottenberg-review-new-museum.html', 'snippet': 'The artist’s new video installation focuses on the strange and sometimes alluring: Siberia, with its warbling throat singers, as well as a potato farm in Maine and the phenomenon known as A.S.M.R.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rustling paper, the crackle of frying food, a whispering voice, beads rubbing together: These are some of the sounds that can induce the brain-tingling sensation known as autonomous sensory meridian response, or A.S.M.R. These kinds of noises are also ubiquitous in the strange and alluring recent videos in Mika Rottenberg’s “Easypieces,” which takes its title from Richard P. Feynman’s book “Six Easy Pieces” (1994): his introduction to the fundamentals of physics for general audiences.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/arts/29mika-review1/29mika-review1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mika Rottenberg’s ‘Easypieces’ Transports You to Parts Unknown', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Journey of Excess Awaits Your Response', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rottenberg, Mika', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-29T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/98b02b42-bf7d-507b-b17a-7085930f4396', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98b02b42-bf7d-507b-b17a-7085930f4396'}, {'abstract': 'The Costes have opened an outpost on the region’s decidedly unglamorous coastline. But outside the confines of their high-design resort, a low-key charm beckons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/29/travel/france-languedoc-beach-vacation.html', 'snippet': 'The Costes have opened an outpost on the region’s decidedly unglamorous coastline. But outside the confines of their high-design resort, a low-key charm beckons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the French painter Gustave Courbet depicted the flat pale gray beach of the Languedoc Coast in “The Seaside at Palavas,” in 1854, it was wild and empty, which is what makes the tiny man in a suit doffing his top hat at the low dark green waves rolling in off the Golfe de Lion so poignant.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28languedoc-france7/28languedoc-france7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28languedoc-france7/28languedoc-france7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28languedoc-france7/28languedoc-france7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28languedoc-france7/28languedoc-france7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1291, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28languedoc-france7/28languedoc-france7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/travel/28languedoc-france7/28languedoc-france7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty