: 'By Miriam Jordan and Caitlin Dickerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miriam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jordan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b2f07c-fac6-5550-a073-62654c7cd64d', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b2f07c-fac6-5550-a073-62654c7cd64d'}, {'abstract': 'Known for her role in the movie “Rabbit-Proof Fence,” she also had a rich stage career, including a critically praised one-woman show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/29/movies/ningali-lawford-wolf-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Known for her role in the movie “Rabbit-Proof Fence,” she also had a rich stage career, including a critically praised one-woman show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ningali Lawford-Wolf, an Indigenous Australian actress who brought the world of her people to the stage and, most notably, to the screen in the film “Rabbit-Proof Fence,” died on Aug. 11 in Edinburgh, where she was touring with the Sydney Theater Company. She was believed to be 52.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/obituaries/30lawfordwolf-01/merlin_159762348_842f0a5a-56c6-4b47-893b-4fdc559fefbc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/30/obituaries/30lawfordwolf-01/merlin_159762348_842f0a5a-56c6-4b47-893b-4fdc559fefbc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/obituaries/30lawfordwolf-01/merlin_159762348_842f0a5a-56c6-4b47-893b-4fdc559fefbc