ths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-theheadlines-australia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-29T17:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Livia Albeck-Ripka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Livia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Albeck-Ripka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/93a6a983-6132-541f-ae36-a4073c04079a', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93a6a983-6132-541f-ae36-a4073c04079a'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, your sex life is influenced by your DNA. But it’s more complicated than that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/29/opinion/genetics-sexual-orientation-study.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, your sex life is influenced by your DNA. But it’s more complicated than that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As researchers in biology and sociology who are also gay men, we have long wondered (and debated) whether sexual orientation has any biological basis. We followed the ascent in the 1990s of the “gay gene” finding — which claimed that male sexual orientation was linked to specific DNA markers — and then watched as that result was called into question. We have wondered whether the two of us, who differ in so many ways, could really trace our common identity to a shared biology.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1298, 'width': 1948, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/29/opinion/29PhelpsWedow/29PhelpsWedow-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Genetics Is Teaching Us About Sexuality', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Genetics Is Teaching Us About Sexuality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-29T18:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven M. Phelps and Robbee Wedow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c525d6b-775b-54f0-b1e0-dc551e8c628a', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c525d6b-775b-54f0-b1e0-dc551e8c628a'}, {'abstract': 'Archaeologists worldwide pooled their knowledge of past land use — and pushed back the date when human farming and other practices began altering the planet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/29/science/archaeology-earth-anthropocene.html', 'snippet': 'Archaeologists worldwide pooled their knowledge of past land use — and pushed back the date when human farming and other practices began altering the planet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Humans substantially altered the planet much earlier than previously thought, a worldwide collection of archaeological experts reported Thursday. By 3,000 years ago, the experts wrote in Science magazine, the planet had been “largely transformed by hunter-gatherers, farmers, and pastoralists.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/03/science/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/03/science/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/03/science/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/03/science/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2/29TB-GLOBALCHANGE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/03/