AN (Harper/HarperCollins, $28.99), Soren Sveistrup’s cunningly plotted Danish police procedural. Caroline Waight’s gruesomely graphic translation of this disturbing account of a body-part-collecting serial killer leaves little to the imagination. A hand here, a foot there — is this guy constructing his own pinup model or are we missing some deeper symbolism?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/01/books/review/01Crime/01Crime-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Body Parts and Missing Bodies: Another Spree of Crime Fiction', 'kicker': 'Crime', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hands Off!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Chestnut Man (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sveistrup, Soren', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waight, Caroline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Bone Fire (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sykes, Sarah (SD Sykes)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Better Man (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Penny, Louise', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Long Call (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cleeves, Ann', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-30T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marilyn Stasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a8582a4-06b2-5c28-9535-2e0be6dda0aa', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a8582a4-06b2-5c28-9535-2e0be6dda0aa'}, {'abstract': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/30/books/review/11-new-books-we-recommend-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve seen our guide to the big books of September, you may already be clearing your schedule in anticipation. But you don’t have to wait: This week’s recommended reading is more than enough