s control the sources of gold used in phones and other devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/30/the-weekly/gold-apple-iphone-colombia.html', 'snippet': 'In Colombia, paramilitary groups control the sources of gold used in phones and other devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re reading this on your phone, you may be holding illegally mined gold from Colombia, where the precious metal has replaced cocaine as the main source of income for organized crime. The growing demand for gold as a conductive metal used in phones and other electronic products has helped spawn a deadly illegal trade that’s harder to track than other black-market commodities like blood diamonds or drugs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Tainted Gold May Have Ended Up in Your Phone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflict Minerals and Resources', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hulu.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duque, Ivan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-08-30T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Universal', 'section_name': 'The Weekly', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de551538-b9bc-5bbe-b1bd-55abd53b8454', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de551538-b9bc-5bbe-b1bd-55abd53b8454'}, {'abstract': 'A hustle play in Hawaii showed why you always play to the whistle — a lesson Oklahoma, Georgia and the Big Ten champ should heed no matter how long the odds get.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/30/sports/ncaafootball/college-football-playoff-alabama-clemson.html', 'snippet': 'A hustle play in Hawaii showed why you always play to the whistle — a lesson Oklahoma, Georgia and the Big Ten champ should heed no matter how long the odds get.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the ball was snapped late Saturday night in Honolulu to Arizona quarterback Khalil Tate from the Hawaii 31-yard line, there were 10 seconds left and the visitors trailed by a touchdown. Hawaii’s Manly Williams focused on his assignment. He lined up over the center, looped around to his left and did his best to keep the dynamic Tate in the pocket.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/sports/30collegefootball-01/30collegefootball-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/30/sports/30collegefootball-01/30collegefootball-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/sports/30collegefootball-01/30collegefootball-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/sports/30collegefootball-01/30collegefootball-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/30/sports/30collegefootball-01/30collegefootball-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/3